{"id":"a92fca03-f0f9-495d-9216-9a2267c28ace","object":"chat.completion","created":1784987433,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError('case must be a dict')\\n    if 'tokens' not in case or 'calls' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError('case must contain tokens and calls')\\n    tokens = case['tokens']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    if not isinstance(tokens, list) or not all(isinstance(t, str) for t in tokens):\\n        raise ValueError('tokens must be a list of strings')\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError('calls must be a list')\\n    # Validate each call\\n    parsed_calls = []\\n    for c in calls:\\n        if not isinstance(c, dict):\\n            raise ValueError('each call must be a dict')\\n        call_id = c.get('call_id')\\n        start = c.get('start')\\n        end = c.get('end')\\n        score = c.get('score')\\n        replacement_tokens = c.get('replacement_tokens')\\n        if not all(x is not None for x in [call_id, start, end, score, replacement_tokens]):\\n            raise ValueError('call missing required fields')\\n        if not isinstance(call_id, str):\\n            raise ValueError('call_id must be a string')\\n        if not isinstance(start, int) or not isinstance(end, int):\\n            raise ValueError('start and end must be integers')\\n        if not (0 <= start < end <= len(tokens)):\\n            raise ValueError('span out of bounds')\\n        if not isinstance(score, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError('score must be numeric')\\n        if not isinstance(replacement_tokens, list) or not all(isinstance(t, str) for t in replacement_tokens):\\n            raise ValueError('replacement_tokens must be a list of strings')\\n        parsed_calls.append({\\n            'call_id': call_id,\\n            'start': start,\\n            'end': end,\\n            'score': score,\\n            'replacement_tokens': replacement_tokens\\n        })\\n    # Sort by descending score, then ascending start, then call_id\\n    sorted_calls = sorted(parsed_calls, key=lambda c: (-c['score'], c['start'], c['call_id']))\\n    # Greedy selection: no overlap\\n    selected = []\\n    for c in sorted_calls:\\n        overlap = False\\n        for s in selected:\\n            if c['start'] < s['end'] and c['end'] > s['start']:\\n                overlap = True\\n                break\\n        if not overlap:\\n            selected.append(c)\\n    # Order selected by source start for reporting\\n    selected.sort(key=lambda c: (c['start'], c['call_id']))\\n    selected_call_ids = [c['call_id'] for c in selected]\\n    # Apply replacements from right to left\\n    ordered_for_apply = sorted(selected, key=lambda c: -c['start'])\\n    result_tokens = list(tokens)  # copy\\n    for c in ordered_for_apply:\\n        result_tokens[c['start']:c['end']] = c['replacement_tokens']\\n    return {\\n        'selected_call_ids': selected_call_ids,\\n        'tokens': result_tokens\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to parse the task: AGENT-TF-02. The function `solve(case)` receives a payload object. Based on the fixture, the payload has \"tokens\" (list of strings), \"calls\" (list of objects with call_id, start, end, score, replacement_tokens). The objective: apply accepted API calls to text while preserving registered span order, rejecting overlaps, and keeping all eligible calls. We must rank candidates by descending score, then start position, then call ID. Greedily reject any span overlapping an already selected span. Order accepted calls by source start for reporting. Apply replacements from right to left so earlier offsets do not shift. Return selected IDs and the exact interleaved token stream.\n\nSo we need to output: selected_call_ids (list of call IDs in order of source start) and tokens (the interleaved token stream after applying replacements).\n\nSteps:\n1. Validate input: ensure tokens is list of strings, calls list of dicts with required fields.\n2. Build list of calls. For each call: call_id, start, end, score, replacement_tokens.\n3. Sort calls by descending score, then ascending start, then call_id (string comparison likely ascending). Greedily select: iterate sorted calls; if the span [start, end) does not overlap with any already selected span (i.e., intervals disjoint; end exclusive? The examples have start inclusive, end exclusive? In fixture: \"start\":1, \"end\":3 means tokens[1] to tokens[2]? Typically Python slicing. Replacement tokens will replace that span. So overlapping means any shared index. Using intervals, we can check if current.start < selected.end and current.end > selected.start). Since we are applying right-to-left, we need to track selected intervals and later apply replacements in decreasing start order.\n4. Collect selected calls, sort by start ascending (and tie? not specified; maybe stable? we can sort by start, then call_id for consistency). \n5. Build tokens list by applying replacements from right to left. That is, sort selected calls by start descending. For each, replace tokens[start:end] with replacement_tokens list. Since we are doing right to left, earlier indices are unaffected.\n6. Return {\"selected_call_ids\": [call_id in order of start], \"tokens\": resulting list}.\n\nEdge cases: overlapping rejection ensures no overlap. If a call's start or end is out of bounds? Assume valid? We'll raise ValueError if invalid.\n\nImplementation: define solve(case). Return dict.\n\nWe'll produce Python source code as a string in JSON.\n\nMake sure to handle optional fields? The schema only specifies tokens and calls in payload. We'll assume they exist.\n\nWe must not mutate case. We'll make deep copies? Not necessary if we only read.\n\nReturn JSON-serializable: list of strings for selected_call_ids, list of strings for tokens.\n\nNow write the code."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1654,"completion_tokens":1388,"total_tokens":3042,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1536},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":606},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":1536,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":118},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}